chapters.Numbers\u000034:
~1 And YHWH spoke to Moses, saying,
~2 “Command the sons of Israel, and say to them: When you⁺ come into the land of Canaan, this [is] the land that shall fall to you⁺ as an inheritance—the land of Canaan to its boundaries:
~3 And your⁺ border on the Negev shall be from the Wilderness of Zin along the border of Edom, and your⁺ border on the Negev shall extend to the end of the Salt Sea eastward.
~4 And your⁺ border shall turn from the Negev to the Ascent of Akrabbim and continue to Zin, and the going forth will be from the Negev to Kadesh-barnea, and it shall go on to Hazar-addar and continue to Azmon.
~5 And the border shall turn from Azmon to the Brook of Egypt, and will be its outer limits to the Sea.
~6 And as for the western border, the Great Sea shall be to you⁺ for a border; this shall be your⁺ western border.
~7 And this shall be your⁺ northern border: From the Great Sea you⁺ shall mark out to you⁺ to Mount Hor.
~8 From Mount Hor you⁺ shall mark out to Lebo-hamath; and the direction of the border shall be toward Zedad;
~9 and the border shall proceed to Ziphron, and it shall end at Hazar-enan. This shall be unto you⁺ the northern border.
~10 And you⁺ shall mark out your⁺ eastern border from Hazar-enan to Shepham,
~11 and the border shall go down from Shepham to Riblah on the east side of Ain, and the border shall go down and reach to the eastern side of the Sea of Chinnereth.
~12 And the border shall go down along the Jordan, and it shall end at the Salt Sea. This shall be to you⁺ the land with its boundaries all around.”
~13 And Moses commanded the sons of Israel, saying, “This [is] the land that you shall inherit by lot, which YHWH has commanded to give to the nine tribes and to the half-tribe;
~14 for the tribe of the sons of the Reubenite has received according to the house of their fathers, and the tribe of the sons of the Gadite according to the house of their fathers, and the half-tribe of Manasseh has received its inheritance.
~15 The two tribes and the half-tribe have received their inheritance on this side of the Jordan [near] Jericho eastward, toward the sunrise.”
~16 And YHWH spoke to Moses, saying,
~17 “These [are] the names of the men who shall divide as an inheritance among you⁺ the land: Eleazar the priest and Joshua son of Nun.
~18 And one leader—one leader from a tribe—you⁺ shall take to distribute the land.
~19 And these [are] the names of the men: From the tribe of Judah, Caleb son of Jephunneh;
~20 and from the tribe of the sons of Simeon, Shemuel son of Ammihud;
~21 from the tribe of Benjamin, Elidad son of Chislon;
~22 and from the tribe of the sons of Dan, a leader Bukki son of Jogli;
~23 from the sons of Joseph, from the tribe of the sons of Manasseh, a leader, Hanniel son of Ephod;
~24 and from the tribe of the sons of Ephraim, a leader, Kemuel son of Shiphtan;
~25 and from the tribe of the sons of Zebulun, a leader, Elizaphan son of Parnach;
~26 and from the tribe of the sons of Issachar, a leader, Paltiel son of Azzan;
~27 and from the tribe of the sons of Asher, a leader, Ahihud son of Shelomi;
~28 and from the tribe of the sons of Naphtali, a leader, Pedahel son of Ammihud.”
~29 These [are] those whom YHWH commanded among the sons of Israel to divide the inheritance in the land of Canaan.

chapters.Deuteronomy\u00008:
~1 Every commandment that I command you today, you⁺ must be careful to do, so that you⁺ may live and multiply and go in and possess the land that YHWH has sworn to your⁺ fathers.
~2 And you shall remember the whole way that YHWH your God led you this forty years in the wilderness, to humble you and test you to know what [was] in your heart, whether you would keep His commandments or not.
~3 And He humbled you and allowed you to hunger, and fed you with manna, which you did not know, nor did your fathers know, so that He might make you know that the man shall not live by bread alone; but by every [word] that proceeds from the mouth of YHWH the man shall live.
~4 Your garments did not wear out from you, and your foot did not swell this forty years.
~5 And you shall know in your heart that as a man disciplines his son, YHWH your God disciplines you.
~6 And you shall keep the commandments of YHWH your God, to walk in His ways and to fear Him.
~7 For YHWH your God is bringing you into a good land, a land of brooks of water, of fountains and springs flowing out of valleys and hills;
~8 a land of wheat, and barley, and vines, and fig trees, and pomegranates; a land of olive oil and honey;
~9 a land in which without scarcity you will eat bread; you will not lack any in it; a land whose stones [are] iron, and from the hills you can dig copper.
~10 And you will eat and be satisfied; and you will bless YHWH your God for the good land that He has given you.
~11 Take heed to it that you do not forget YHWH your God, by not keeping His commandments and His ordinances and His statutes, which I command you today—
~12 lest you eat and be satisfied and build and inhabit beautiful houses;
~13 and your herd and your flock multiply, and your silver and your gold multiply to you, and all that [is] to you is multiplied;
~14 and your heart is lifted up, and you forget YHWH your God, who brought you out of the land of Egypt, from the house of slavery;
~15 who led you in the great and the terrible wilderness, [with] fiery serpents and scorpions and thirsty land where there was no water; who brought water for you out of the rock of flint;
~16 who fed you in the wilderness with manna that your fathers did not know, so that He might humble you, that He might test you, to do you good in the end;
~17 and you say in your heart, “My power and the might of my hand have gained me this wealth.”
~18 And you shall remember YHWH your God, for He gives you power to gain wealth, that He may establish His covenant that He swore to your fathers, as [it is] this day.
~19 And it shall come to pass, if you ever forget YHWH your God and follow after other gods, and serve them and worship them, I testify against you⁺ this day that you⁺ will surely perish.
~20 As the nations that YHWH destroys before you⁺, so you⁺ shall perish, because you⁺ would not listen to the voice of YHWH your⁺ God.

